# DECISION_GRAPH — {{PROJECT_NAME}}

> **Purpose.** The graph of *judgments*: what was decided, why, what was
> rejected, and what each decision constrains. The third leg of the knowledge
> fabric — SKILL_GRAPH stores *how*, SCARS stores *what breaks*, this file
> stores *why*. A project's intelligence is procedures + failures + judgments;
> without the third, every new agent re-litigates the past.
>
> **Contract for every agent (any runtime).**
> 1. NEVER re-open a `decided` node. If new evidence truly changes the picture,
>    add a `pending` node that PROPOSES superseding it — the decider flips it.
> 2. NEVER act silently where a `pending` node exists on your path — act on its
>    recorded default if one is stated, otherwise escalate to the decider.
> 3. When your work surfaces a decision only the owner can make, APPEND a
>    `pending` node with the options and evidence — in the same slice as the
>    work that surfaced it.
> 4. Cite decision ids (`D-<slug>`) in commits that implement them.
>
> **Status flow:** `pending → decided → superseded` (never deleted).
>
> **Update trigger:** any owner/irreversible decision — same commit as the
> work it gates.

